control: A process serves its application server over TLS when its configuration names a key pair and over plain HTTP when it names neither, with the key pair read from its mounted files, and refuses to start with one of the two or with a pair that does not load
removes: the application server is served over TLS even when the configuration names no key pair, so a process given neither file never serves
packages: ./process/host
tests: TestTheApplicationServerGivenNoKeyPairIsPlain/neither_file TestTheApplicationServerGivenNoKeyPairIsPlain/both_blank
scheduled-count: no

